      "title": "Allgemeine Sicherheitsregeln im Chemielabor anwenden",
      "authorDisposition": "keep_removal_no_replacement",
      "addExistingPrerequisiteIds": [],
      "rationale": "This is the introductory safe-preparation and immediate-response competency itself. Both actual tasks use a harmless supervised water station or a splash-response card; no weighing, separation, recovery or laboratory-method performance must already be mastered. Preserve its existing orientation inheritance; do not make safety conditional on broad methods.",
      "counterexampleBoundary": "A learner can prepare the labelled station, reject an unknown vessel and give the correct splash response while unable to weigh/filter or calculate recovery.",
